+## Phase 4c — Preference resolutions (last 10 runs)
+
+```bash
+jq -s '
+  map(select(.kind == "askuser_resolved"))
+  | sort_by(.ts) | reverse | .[0:10]
+  | {
+      total: length,
+      by_result: (
+        group_by(.result)
+        | map({(.[0].result // "unknown"): length})
+        | add // {}
+      ),
+      by_source: (
+        group_by(.source)
+        | map({(.[0].source // "unknown"): length})
+        | add // {}
+      ),
+      by_question_id: (
+        group_by(.question_id)
+        | map({key: (.[0].question_id // "unknown"), count: length})
+        | sort_by(-.count)
+      ),
+      conflict_count: (map(select(.source == "conflict")) | length)
+    }
+' "$METRICS"
+```
+
+Display as a human-readable section:
+
+```
+Preference resolutions (last 10 runs):
+  Total: <N>
+  By result:  skip=<N>  prefill=<N>  ask=<N>
+  By source:  config=<N>  memory=<N>  conflict=<N>  none=<N>  override=<N>
+  By question (most-fired first):
+    workflow.audit_to_amend    <N>
+    workflow.slug_confirm      <N>
+  Conflict rate: <conflict_count>/<total> (<pct>%)  ← proxy for user surprise; trend down as TOML stabilises
+```
+
+Rules for display:
+- Only show non-zero result/source buckets.
+- Omit `By question` rows with count 0.
+- Conflict rate line: if total is 0, print `  (no askuser_resolved events found in metrics.jsonl)` and skip the rest.
+- Conflict rate percentage: `round(conflict_count / total * 100)`. Show `0%` when conflict_count is 0.
+- Read-only; no writes.
+
 ## Phase 5 — Stalls (post-run gap detection)
 
 Reuse the gap-detection awk from `/z-implement-all` Detecting Stalls section. Flag any gap > 30 min between consecutive same-run events.
